# A copy under the negation of its presence test.
-- source.cue --
c?: string
-- target.cue --
a: string
-- lens.cue --
input: _
result: {if input.c == _|_ {a: input.c}}
-- out --
not total
result.a copies input.c, which may be absent: input.c is optional in the source schema; guard the field with if input.c != _|_ (rule source-absent) @ lens.cue:2:32
result.a is required by the target schema, and is written only under input.c == _|_, which the checker cannot show cover every instance; write it unconditionally, under a condition and its negation, or under type tests covering every alternative of the tested field (rule unknown-coverage) @ lens.cue:2:1
